# nibarc - nibar configuration
#
# Copy to ~/.config/niwm/nibarc. Unlike niwmrc, you only need the lines
# you want to change: everything left out keeps its default, shown here.
# Desktop themes (nni theme) set the colours through X resources; a colour
# you set here wins over the theme.
# Reload with mod+ctrl+r (niwm's reload) or `pkill -HUP nibar`.
# Flags given to nibar on the command line win over this file.

# ---- placement ------------------------------------------------------------
# position left            # left or right edge
# width 150                # pixels, 80 to 600
# monitor 1                # which monitor (1 = the primary). For a bar on
#                          # each monitor, start one per monitor: nibar -m 2

# What happens when a window goes fullscreen:
#   below   it covers the bar (the default)
#   above   the bar stays on top of it
#   beside  it shrinks to fill the screen next to the bar
# layer below

# ---- colours ----------------------------------------------------------------
# background #161214
# foreground #e8dcd8
# The accent (viewed tag, focus stripe, menu border, the chicken's comb),
# the border lines and the urgent colour follow niwm's focus_color,
# normal_color and urgent_color unless you give a colour here.
# accent auto
# border auto
# urgent auto

# font -misc-fixed-medium-r-semicondensed--13-*-*-*-*-*-iso10646-1

# ---- sections -----------------------------------------------------------------
# logo yes                 # the chicken on the menu button
# logo_color auto          # the chicken's body; auto = the text colour
# label Apps               # text on the menu button
# windows viewed           # viewed: windows on the viewed tags; all: every window
# battery yes
# network yes
# clock 24h                # 24h, 12h or off
# date %a %d %b            # strftime format, or off

# ---- system tray ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Icons from apps like nm-applet, volume controls or chat apps.
# tray yes
# tray_size 18             # pixels, 12 to 48
#
# Choose icons by their class name. nibar prints each icon's class when it
# docks, to wherever niwm's output goes (see `man niwm`, ~/.niwm.log).
# Names can be listed on one line or over several lines.
# tray_hide Blueman-applet Pasystray     # never show these
# tray_show Nm-applet                    # if given, show only these
